course: dictionary
lesson: 14527
title: Perpetrate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Perpetrate is a formal word meaning to do something wrong, harmful or illegal, such as a crime or a trick. It changes its ending like other verbs: perpetrates, perpetrated, perpetrating. The person who does it is the perpetrator.
explain: «The thieves perpetrated the robbery at the bank last night.» The clue is robbery, which is a crime, so perpetrated means carried out. Try swapping in did: the sentence still works, but perpetrate sounds more serious and formal.
explain: Detectives in mystery stories work out who perpetrated the crime. News reports and history books use the word too. People sometimes use it as a joke, such as «Who perpetrated this terrible pun?», where it just means who made it.
fact: Perpetrate means to do something wrong, harmful or illegal.
fact: Perpetrate is a formal word, so you will often find it in news, law and history.
fact: The person who perpetrates a crime is called the perpetrator.
fact: «Perpetrated» is the past tense: «The fraud was perpetrated last year.»
fact: As a joke, «Who perpetrated this terrible pun?» means who made it.
exercise: «The thief perpetrated the theft at the bank.» What does perpetrated mean? | Painted | *Carried out a crime | Ran away from | Gave a gift to
exercise: In a crime story, who is the perpetrator? | The police officer who arrests people | The friend who helped the hero | The judge in the court | *The person who did the crime
exercise: Which word is a formal word meaning to do something wrong? | Persuade | Permit | Pretend | *Perpetrate
test: «The gang perpetrated a robbery in the night.» Which word means the person who did it? | *Perpetrator | Witness | Victim | Detective
test: In «Who perpetrated this terrible pun?», what does perpetrated mean? | Broken | *Made or done | Sold | Stolen
exam: Which word means to do something wrong or illegal? | Permit | Prefer | Protect | *Perpetrate
